{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 36, :comments ["<b>To give them on the day of their anointing</b> — its full reading: which HaShem commanded on the day of anointing them, to give them from the children of Israel, an everlasting statute. And the meaning of \"on the day of anointing\" is at the time of the anointing, and likewise \"on the day he presented them to serve as priests\" (Leviticus 7:35) — at that time when He set them apart. And Rabbi Abraham said (Ibn Ezra on Leviticus 7:36) that \"on the day of anointing\" means from the day of anointing, and likewise \"that which remains of the flesh and of the bread\" (Leviticus 8:32)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:51:27.639819008Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}